[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (-10000) is (277), original query: (Viruses are considered an exception to the cell theory because they), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(11.366225036741548), 'The endosymbiotic theory suggests that mitochondria and chloroplasts were once independent, free-living prokaryotes. The correct answer that does NOT support this theory is: Mitochondria and chloroplasts function independently from the eukaryotic host cell. This option is incorrect because mitochondria and chloroplasts are now dependent on the eukaryotic host cell and do not function independently.'), (np.float64(10.990194714553247), 'An animal cell that is permeable to water but not salts has an internal NaCl concentration of 10%. If placed in freshwater, the cell will swell and eventually lyse. This is because the cell membrane allows water to enter the cell, causing it to swell, but the concentration of salts remains constant, leading to a dilution of the cells internal environment, ultimately causing the cell to lyse.'), (np.float64(10.486572578353702), 'The correct answer is Fibroblast cells. Fibroblast cells are a type of cell that plays a role in the production of collagen and other structural proteins, but they are not directly involved in controlling cell division. The other options, Cyclins, Protein kinases, and Checkpoints, are all known to play important roles in regulating the cell division process.')])
