[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (-10000) is (277), original query: (Which of the following statements is correct about the DNA content of a particular diploid cell just prior to mitosis if the DNA content of the same diploid cell in G1 is X?), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(36.03038466894661), 'Asexual reproduction in animals is characterized by daughter cells having the same number of chromosomes as the parent cell, being identical to the parent cell, and the parent cell producing diploid cells. In contrast, in asexual reproduction, the daughter cells do not fuse to form a zygote, which is a characteristic of sexual reproduction.'), (np.float64(35.170674542715375), 'The correct answer is S for the phase in which the quantity of DNA in a eukaryotic cell typically doubles. This occurs during the S phase of the cell cycle, where the DNA replication process takes place.'), (np.float64(30.583565261843415), 'An animal cell that is permeable to water but not salts has an internal NaCl concentration of 10%. If placed in freshwater, the cell will swell and eventually lyse. This is because the cell membrane allows water to enter the cell, causing it to swell, but the concentration of salts remains constant, leading to a dilution of the cells internal environment, ultimately causing the cell to lyse.')])
