[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (-10000) is (277), original query: (A scientist carries out a cross between two guinea pigs, both of which have black coats. Black hair coat is dominant over white hair coat. Three quarters of the offspring have black coats, and one quarter have white coats. The genotypes of the parents were most likely), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(49.4094620876807), 'In a population of guinea pigs, 4% are black (recessive) and 96% are brown. The heterozygous condition, which is the combination of the two alleles, has a frequency of 32%.'), (np.float64(43.29000646209708), 'A rooster and hen with gray feathers produced 17 gray, 7 black, and 8 white chicks. The simplest explanation for the inheritance of these colors is that the traits for black and white demonstrate incomplete dominance, meaning that the effect of one gene is not completely masked by the other.'), (np.float64(36.68495328596186), 'In Labrador retrievers, two genes determine coat color: one for melanin (B and b) and one for pigment deposition (E and e). The dominant allele B codes for black fur, while b codes for brown hair. The E allele is epistatic to the B/b gene, meaning it overrides the effects of the melanin gene if present. Therefore, if the dominant E allele is present, the coat color will be yellow, regardless of the genotype at the melanin locus.')])
