[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (263), original query: (The end product of the alcohol fermentation pathway is the alcohol ethanol. A considerable amount of energy still remains in ethanol, yet ethanol is a waste product for the yeast cells that produce it. What, then, is the purpose of fermentation?), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(37.71910764658428), 'When oxygen becomes unavailable, fermentation regenerates NAD+, allowing cellular respiration to continue. Fermentation is the process by which cells generate energy in the absence of oxygen. This is the correct answer, as it is the mechanism by which cells can continue to produce energy when oxygen is not available.'), (np.float64(32.39097464518188), 'The incorrect statement about post-transcriptional modification is that a guanine cap is added to the 5′ end of the mRNA.'), (np.float64(32.176932705937155), 'The correct answer is that oxidative phosphorylation harvests the most energy because it transfers the potential energy stored in NADH and FADH to ATP, resulting in the production of a significant amount of ATP.')])
