[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (92), original query: (Which of these evolutionary agents is most consistent at causing populations to become better suited to their environments over the course of generations?), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(20.11231993578262), 'Fossil records show that horses have evolved to become larger over time. This trend is an example of directional selection, where a population adapts to its environment by becoming larger, resulting in a consistent direction of change.'), (np.float64(18.235813305969238), 'A population is considered the evolutionary unit because individuals cannot evolve on their own, but populations can. This is because genetic changes occur at the population level, not at the individual level.'), (np.float64(18.203641822663663), 'According to the text, the correct answer is Populations tend to increase at a faster rate than their food supply normally allows. This idea was learned by Charles Darwin from the writings of Thomas Malthus.')])
