[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (11), original query: (Compared to DNA viral replication, RNA viral replication is more susceptible to mutation because), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(15.706964989854677), 'Viral transduction is the process by which viruses transfer bacterial DNA from one bacterial cell to another. This process plays a crucial role in bacterial evolution by increasing genetic variation of the bacteria.'), (np.float64(13.851512471290262), 'Some viruses can transform normal mammalian cells into cancer cells in vitro. The correct answer is NOT any of the options listed, which include the formation of a pilus between the cell and virus, the incorporation of viral DNA into the cells nuclear DNA, or the conversion of the hosts genome into viral DNA.'), (np.float64(13.483012567522914), 'If two modern organisms are distantly related in an evolutionary sense, one would expect them to share fewer homologous structures compared to more closely related organisms. This is because distantly related organisms have had more time to accumulate changes and diverge from a common ancestor.')])
