[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (55), original query: (Destruction of all beta cells in the pancreas will cause which of the following to occur?), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(16.35382182344539), 'The correct answer to the question All of the following play a role in morphogenesis EXCEPT is operons, which is incorrect. Morphogenesis, the process of tissue formation, involves apoptosis (programmed cell death), homeotic genes, and inductive effects.'), (np.float64(15.340022455264721), 'The correct answer to the question Which aspects of cell structure best reveals the unity of all life? is All cells are surrounded by a plasma membrane. This is because all living organisms, from bacteria to humans, have a plasma membrane that surrounds their cells, indicating a shared characteristic among all living things.'), (np.float64(14.951180266137886), 'A chemical agent that denatures all enzymes in the synaptic cleft will prevent the degradation of acetylcholine. This means that acetylcholine will not be broken down and will remain in the synaptic cleft, but it will still be released from the presynaptic membrane and bind to receptor proteins on the postsynaptic membrane.')])
