[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (4), original query: (Similar evolutionary changes occurring in two species that can be related or unrelated.), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(15.498123694905335), 'If two modern organisms are distantly related in an evolutionary sense, one would expect them to share fewer homologous structures compared to more closely related organisms. This is because distantly related organisms have had more time to accumulate changes and diverge from a common ancestor.'), (np.float64(13.307641170343185), 'Divergent evolution occurs when two related species evolve in a way that makes them less similar over time. This process is the opposite of convergent evolution, where unrelated species evolve to become more similar.'), (np.float64(12.458178013884636), 'Convergent evolution is the process by which two unrelated species evolve to become more similar over time, often in response to similar environmental pressures or selection forces. This occurs when different species develop similar traits or characteristics, such as body shape or physiology, in order to adapt to their environments in similar ways.')])
