[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (255), original query: (A child with type A B blood inherits an IA allele from one parent and an IB allele from the other. The child will carry both A and B glycoproteins on the surface of all red blood cells. This pattern of expression is referred to as), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(48.2739362548069), 'The question states that a couple with type B and AB blood have a child. The correct answer is that the probability the child has type O blood is 0%. This is because type O blood is recessive and can only occur if both parents are O or have the O allele, which is not the case in this scenario.'), (np.float64(38.264448447751704), 'In a population with an autosomal gene previously fixed for one allele, a new allele is introduced through mutation and natural selection causes stabilizing selection. Over many generations, both the proportion of homozygotes for each allele and the populations average heterozygosity will increase.'), (np.float64(37.402505415284104), 'In Labrador retrievers, two genes determine coat color: one for melanin (B and b) and one for pigment deposition (E and e). The dominant allele B codes for black fur, while b codes for brown hair. The E allele is epistatic to the B/b gene, meaning it overrides the effects of the melanin gene if present. Therefore, if the dominant E allele is present, the coat color will be yellow, regardless of the genotype at the melanin locus.')])
