[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (233), original query: (There are 40 individuals in population 1, all of which have genotype A1A1, and there are 25 individuals in population 2, all of genotype A2A2. Assume that these populations are located far from one another and that their environmental conditions are very similar. Based on the information given here, the observed genetic variation is mostly likely an example of), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(36.860519564191804), 'The correct statement about variation is not among the given options. The incorrect options are: All phenotypic variation is the result of genotypic variation., All genetic variation produces phenotypic variation., and All new alleles are the result of nucleotide variability.'), (np.float64(34.25871721956746), 'The correct answer is Poorly adapted individuals never produce offspring. This option is not an observation or inference on which natural selection is based. The other options are all correct: there is heritable variation among individuals, species produce more offspring than the environment can support, and individuals with characteristics best suited to the environment generally leave more offspring than those less suited.'), (np.float64(33.73128008555784), 'The correct answer to the question Natural selection is based on all of the following except is not genetic variation exists within populations, as this is a fundamental aspect of natural selection. The correct answer is actually one of the other options, which are: the best-adapted individuals tend to leave the most offspring, individuals who survive longer tend to leave more offspring than those who die young, or individuals adapt to their environments and, thereby, evolve.')])
