[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (226), original query: (Crop rotation is the successive planting of different crops on the same land in sequential seasons. Which of the following statements summarizes the most likely benefits of this practice?), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(25.547768853868494), 'Crossover (recombination) is most likely to occur when two genes are located on the same chromosome, but not next to each other. This is because the process of crossing over happens when the homologous chromosomes exchange genetic material, which is more likely to happen when the genes are on the same chromosome.'), (np.float64(23.961437371741596), 'The correct answer to the question Which of the following describes a symbiotic relationship? is: Remora fish eat parasites off of sharks; the sharks stay free of parasites, and the remora fish are protected from predators. This is an example of a symbiotic relationship, where one species (remora fish) benefits from the other (sharks) and vice versa.'), (np.float64(23.584718477917875), 'Incomplete dominance and epistasis are two genetic concepts. Incomplete dominance refers to the interaction of two alleles on the same gene, where one allele is not completely dominant over the other. Epistasis, on the other hand, describes the interaction of two different genes, where the effect of one gene affects the expression of the other.')])
