[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (193), original query: (Monkeys of South and Central America have prehensile tails, meaning that their tails can be used to grasp objects. The tails of African and Asian monkeys are not prehensile. Which discipline is most likely to provide an evolutionary explanation for how this difference in tails came about?), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(29.63277918177364), 'Bacteria and yeast cells need to maintain homeostasis of their plasma membrane in a temperature-varying environment. One viable strategy is to change the ratio of phospholipids with double covalent bonds in their tails to those without double covalent bonds. This helps to maintain the fluidity of the plasma membrane, which can vary in response to temperature changes.'), (np.float64(27.31185000735292), 'Ichthyosaurs, aquatic dinosaurs, had dorsal fins and tails like fish, despite their terrestrial reptile relatives lacking these features. The similarities between ichthyosaurs and fish are due to B and C, which are incorrect answers.'), (np.float64(22.81014135159316), 'Most animal cells are relatively small and uniform in size, which is due to the fact that smaller cells have a larger surface-to-volume ratio. This is the correct answer, meaning that the surface area of the cell is proportionally larger compared to its volume, allowing for more efficient exchange of materials and energy.')])
