[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (229), original query: (Which of the following statements is correct about a man who has hemophilia and whose wife does not have the disease and who does not have any relatives with the disease?), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(24.421696605857647), 'The correct answer to the question Natural selection is based on all of the following except is not genetic variation exists within populations, as this is a fundamental aspect of natural selection. The correct answer is actually one of the other options, which are: the best-adapted individuals tend to leave the most offspring, individuals who survive longer tend to leave more offspring than those who die young, or individuals adapt to their environments and, thereby, evolve.'), (np.float64(24.371406760858775), 'The correct answer is not among the options provided. The group composed entirely of individuals who maintained that species are fixed (i.e., unchanging) is not Aristotle, Cuvier, and Lamarck.'), (np.float64(23.389151957389068), 'The correct answer is actually not Subsequent generations of a population should have greater proportions of individuals that possess traits better suited for success. This statement is not an inference of natural selection. Natural selection is the process by which individuals with favorable traits are more likely to survive and reproduce, but it does not necessarily guarantee that subsequent generations will have a greater proportion of individuals with those traits.')])
