[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (53), original query: (A cell is placed into a hypertonic environment and its cytoplasm shrivels up. This demonstrates the principle of), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(17.612612296719043), 'An AP Biology student placed a dialysis bag with a 0.5 M solution into a beaker with a 0.6 M solution. If the bag were placed in distilled water instead, the expected result would be a net flow of water into the bag, causing it to swell in size.'), (np.float64(16.108726950377626), 'An animal cell that is permeable to water but not salts has an internal NaCl concentration of 10%. If placed in freshwater, the cell will swell and eventually lyse. This is because the cell membrane allows water to enter the cell, causing it to swell, but the concentration of salts remains constant, leading to a dilution of the cells internal environment, ultimately causing the cell to lyse.'), (np.float64(15.407795001724123), 'Some viruses can transform normal mammalian cells into cancer cells in vitro. The correct answer is NOT any of the options listed, which include the formation of a pilus between the cell and virus, the incorporation of viral DNA into the cells nuclear DNA, or the conversion of the hosts genome into viral DNA.')])
