[VectorDB] search done, count of bm25 score higher than (10) is (8), original query: (The tandem back-and-forth evolution of closely related species, which is exemplified by predator-prey relationships.), scored_docs: ([(np.float64(15.941673231366584), 'Convergent evolution is best exemplified by the similarity between the wings of an insect and a bird, despite being from different species and having different evolutionary paths.'), (np.float64(11.781081074101484), 'The sequence of amino acids in human hemoglobin is more similar to that of chimpanzees than to dogs, indicating that humans and chimpanzees are more closely related than humans and dogs. This suggests that the two species share a more recent common ancestor.'), (np.float64(11.711042633740567), 'The observation that island organisms are distinct but closely related to similar species on the nearest continent suggests that the islands were originally part of the continent. This implies that the same organisms inhabited the common environment, supporting option 0, common environments are inhabited by the same organisms.')])
